{% extends "@core/base.p2" %}

{% comment %}
  Sign-in form.

  The fields have no classes on them at all. Pico styles a block-level input that
  follows a label, which is both what a form should be marked up like and what
  makes this page survive a redesign of the stylesheet: there is no class name
  here for a rename to orphan.

  The form posts to itself and the password field is never repopulated. A
  framework that remembered a submitted password so the user could "try again"
  would write it into the browser's form state, and into whatever a misconfigured
  cache stored of the page.

  The failure message is one value for every reason the attempt failed, and it is
  the caller's job to pass that one value: the difference between "no such
  account" and "wrong password" is what an enumeration attack reads. It is marked
  as an alert rather than coloured, because Pico ships no alert styling and the
  thing a failure has to communicate is that it replaced what the user was
  doing, which is a job for the accessibility tree rather than for a background
  colour.
{% endcomment %}

{% block title %}Sign in · {{ siteTitle|default:"Application" }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<article>
  <header>
    <h1>Sign in</h1>
  </header>

  {% if loginError %}
  <p role="alert">{{ loginError }}</p>
  {% endif %}

  <form method="post" action="{{ action|default:'/login' }}">
    {{ csrfInput }}

    <label for="wa-username">
      Username
      <input
        type="text"
        id="wa-username"
        name="username"
        value="{{ username|default:'' }}"
        autocomplete="username"
        autocapitalize="none"
        spellcheck="false"
        required>
    </label>

    <label for="wa-password">
      Password
      <input
        type="password"
        id="wa-password"
        name="password"
        autocomplete="current-password"
        required>
    </label>

    {% if next %}<input type="hidden" name="next" value="{{ next }}">{% endif %}

    <button type="submit">Sign in</button>
  </form>
</article>
{% endblock %}
